            <div xml:id="d368">

                <pb facs="0698" n="562" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg562"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79611 Pan American Airways, Inc./476:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Venezuela</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-06-12T18:00:00-04:30">June 12, 1929—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>61. Department’s 18, May 25, 3 p.m. Foreign Office in a note dated today
                    transmits without comment letter from Minister of Fomento, also of today,
                    granting permission for one more flight “with official correspondence”.</p>
                <p>… I therefore suggest the Legation be instructed to repeat request for temporary
                    operating permit.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
